nch-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/6b4d617df080cef71cd8f4b041601cf47ce0edf3/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "members_read_calls": 1, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nApplying the fixes.\n[tool: bash]\nLine 3 of `catalog/members.py`, quoted verbatim:\n\n> `# The lending policy allows each member to hold five books at once.`\n\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` ran 16 tests, all OK. It was 15 before because `test_search` couldn't be imported at all. I didn't change any tests.\n\nWhat I fixed:\n- **`catalog/members.py:4`**: the borrowing limit was set to 3, but the comment on line 3 and the tests both say five. I changed it to 5.\n- **`catalog/search.py:3`**: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`, a module that doesn't exist. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`catalog/fees.py:14`**: the fee was days late *plus* the daily fee. It's now days late *times* the daily fee.\n- **`catalog/inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`catalog/books.py:22`**: `parse_book` stored the year as text, which also broke `age()`. It now stores it as a number.\n- **`catalog/factory.py`**: the demo catalog was missing `Emma`, which the docstring and tests expect. The tests only check the title, so I picked the other details myself: `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 32831, "requests_cache_write": 64359, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3568252, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "re